    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜ことができます: being able to do something",
     "texto": [
      "Another, more formal way of saying you can do something: dictionary-form verb + **こと が できます**: **にほんご を はなす こと が できます** (I can speak Japanese).",
      "**こと** means «thing, act» and here it turns the verb into a noun."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜の が すき です: I like doing",
     "texto": [
      "To say what you like doing, dictionary-form verb + **の が すき です**: **うた を うたう の が すき です** (I like singing).",
      "With **の** you turn the verb into a noun and give **が** the role of subject."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜の が じょうず です: being good at",
     "texto": [
      "To say you do it well, use the same pattern with **じょうず**: **りょうり が じょうず です** (I'm good at cooking).",
      "Note: **じょうず** is a -na adjective: you say **じょうず です**, not **じょうずい**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
